    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1784">

                <pb facs="1164" n="1048" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg1048"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.74/57.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Price to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 23, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to my cable of August 14, Department’s telegram August 17. We have
                    taken and are exercising complete control of wireless <pb facs="1165" n="1049"
                        xml:id="pg1049"/> pursuant to verbal authority from Panama; but the decree
                    of Panaman President assured me for August 14 was submitted only last Tuesday.
                    It gave only temporary control during the crisis in Europe. Under my protest its
                    publication was withheld and Panaman Minister for Foreign Affairs agreed to have
                    it reformed, granting complete and permanent control in accordance with prior
                    assurances.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Price</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
